From 968d2acc0d823df13de36808a22ad3f0222844f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 22:19:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 170/638] chrome: own AROS profiles through an Exec port
 [chromium] [aros]

Statement: The POSIX process singleton depends on Unix-domain sockets, filesystem locks, and PID probing that AROS does not provide.

Decision: Represent each browser profile with a public Exec MsgPort named from a stable FNV-1a hash of its user-data path. Register ownership atomically under Forbid/Permit and reject a second process without claiming command forwarding support.

Evidence: The real //chrome:chrome graph selected process_singleton_posix.cc and could not express profile ownership on AROS.

Validation: process_singleton_aros.o compiles in the symbol-free out/aros-chrome target graph.

Chain:; ACD-chromium-aros-native-window-system
